WEBVTT

00:01.380 --> 00:04.080
There's one thing you need to get straight.

00:04.750 --> 00:06.880
This is our battle!

00:07.210 --> 00:10.460
The battle between those of us
who chose to flee and survive

00:10.460 --> 00:13.750
and the dragons who are out to kill us!

00:14.040 --> 00:15.290
But you?

00:15.460 --> 00:16.380
Listen up.

00:16.380 --> 00:18.380
No matter how strong you are,

00:18.380 --> 00:21.250
or how fantastic your reason to fight is,

00:21.630 --> 00:23.630
you can't just show up late

00:23.630 --> 00:25.830
and act like you're the hero!

00:27.960 --> 00:29.960
Princess-Style Barrier Arts!

00:30.420 --> 00:31.420
Cage!

00:32.830 --> 00:36.790
Did you think drawing me into the woods
would give you the advantage, Olto Zora?

00:37.040 --> 00:41.250
In that case, I'll simply transform
this forest into my territory!

00:41.250 --> 00:43.670
Yes, yes! We did it, we did it!

00:43.670 --> 00:46.250
All that magic is just pouring in!

00:46.380 --> 00:48.630
Our biggest advantage is that
we don't need to win.

00:48.630 --> 00:50.420
We only need to kill dragons and survive

00:50.420 --> 00:53.380
until we've accumulated enough magic
to teleport all of us.

00:53.380 --> 00:54.380
But...

00:54.630 --> 00:57.750
During my time as a Solarian,

00:57.750 --> 01:03.460
they were researching possibly stealing
dragons' magic and using it in battle.

01:03.460 --> 01:07.880
And now I'm witnessing that research
being successfully implemented...

01:08.290 --> 01:10.880
Although, I'm on the dragons' side now.

01:12.540 --> 01:15.380
I've got your little plan all figured out!

01:21.790 --> 01:25.790
The Silverware Princess' eyes can perceive
the aura emitted by all creation.

01:26.710 --> 01:29.290
However, dragons do not emit auras.

01:29.880 --> 01:35.080
But that doesn't mean the Silverware Princess'
senses cannot recognize dragons.

01:35.750 --> 01:40.880
They appear as black masses obstructing
the glow from a world brimming with light.

01:40.880 --> 01:43.380
In this way, she can identify dragons.

01:43.920 --> 01:48.460
However, this is a forest turned draconic,
the Writhing Shade.

01:48.460 --> 01:52.130
Everything in the vicinity is completely black.

01:52.130 --> 01:54.130
Here, she can't perceive
the movements of dragons.

01:54.580 --> 01:57.580
Consequently, the movements of
the people under Olto Zora's control

01:57.580 --> 02:00.960
tipped her off that something was wrong.

02:02.540 --> 02:05.210
The enemy's human force is moving.

02:05.830 --> 02:07.330
Is this random?

02:07.500 --> 02:09.330
No, they're...

02:09.790 --> 02:15.080
You can only teleport humans
that are within its area of effect.

02:15.080 --> 02:17.920
Or that's how I imagine your
magic circle is configured.

02:17.920 --> 02:22.250
They're avoiding our troops
as they approach the base.

02:24.080 --> 02:28.080
You'll have to collect double
the amount of magic to teleport!

02:28.500 --> 02:30.170
They're sabotaging our teleportation!

02:30.170 --> 02:31.380
That was quick!

02:31.380 --> 02:32.790
He's already onto us!

04:03.500 --> 04:09.080
<b>Episode 14: Impatience and Vigilance</b>

04:04.960 --> 04:06.000
Their magic is coming!

04:06.000 --> 04:07.630
Prepare for any abnormal-

04:07.630 --> 04:09.330
Blood is flame.

04:12.460 --> 04:14.170
Princess-Style Barrier Arts!

04:14.170 --> 04:15.290
Shield!

04:17.500 --> 04:20.040
Wh-what's this power?

04:20.040 --> 04:25.460
Inferior and medial dragons who have lived
long enough to become experienced...

04:27.750 --> 04:29.380
Those belong to that spikey prick!

04:29.380 --> 04:34.380
...learn the same magic as
the mature dragon who created them.

04:35.630 --> 04:36.710
Gunners!

04:36.710 --> 04:38.170
Can you aim from the sky?

04:40.710 --> 04:43.460
Listen to the voice of the wind.

04:44.420 --> 04:48.710
These are the perfected pawns
of our bloodline.

04:49.790 --> 04:51.330
Mature dragons.

04:51.710 --> 04:53.880
Dozens of elite dragon hunters

04:53.880 --> 04:59.960
have to work together to kill a single
mature dragon, and we've got...

04:59.960 --> 05:01.330
Oh! Em! Gee!

05:01.330 --> 05:02.960
What luck!

05:02.960 --> 05:05.250
Today's the big beastie blowout sale!

05:05.580 --> 05:08.500
We managed to get our hands on forty!

05:11.000 --> 05:12.540
Protective Barrier!

05:14.710 --> 05:17.960
Nothing from the outside may pass through.

05:17.960 --> 05:21.040
Everything inside may pass through.

05:24.540 --> 05:29.380
I estimate that the magic absorption
circle's range is two kilometers.

05:29.380 --> 05:31.330
That surpasses the level

05:31.330 --> 05:34.330
that a magically undeveloped country
can independently create.

05:34.580 --> 05:38.830
Something is behind this, undoubtably.

05:39.580 --> 05:44.920
I didn't see her face, but there was a
white-haired woman wearing a black dress.

05:44.920 --> 05:46.880
And the magic she was using...

05:46.880 --> 05:50.170
I think it was greater than my Barrier Magic.

05:50.580 --> 05:52.750
We have the upper hand.

05:52.750 --> 05:56.380
But numerous things happened that were
beyond the scope of my expectations.

05:56.380 --> 05:59.960
It's possible this situation
could be reversed in a flash.

05:59.960 --> 06:03.880
After all, no matter how victorious
we are in this war,

06:03.880 --> 06:06.630
it's a defeat for us if the princess escapes.

06:06.630 --> 06:10.790
It's possible she'll realize
there's no hope of winning,

06:10.790 --> 06:15.500
abandon the civilians,
and activate the teleportation magic.

06:16.040 --> 06:18.920
In order to decisively win this,

06:18.920 --> 06:21.830
we'll take control of
the magic circle in the base.

06:21.830 --> 06:23.880
That's our top priority.

06:26.380 --> 06:30.380
All our soldiers on the front line
suddenly died!

06:31.000 --> 06:33.540
I didn't witness the moment they died.

06:33.920 --> 06:36.290
Even though I was watching them.

06:36.630 --> 06:40.000
Before I knew it, they were dead,
and blood was pooling under them.

06:40.250 --> 06:42.170
They had no life left in them.

06:42.750 --> 06:45.170
I don't know what happened.

06:45.170 --> 06:47.540
But I know that thing...

06:48.040 --> 06:49.500
is responsible.

06:59.330 --> 07:01.170
The barrier disappeared!

07:01.500 --> 07:02.210
No!

07:02.540 --> 07:03.880
No way!

07:04.290 --> 07:07.080
Parts of the wall have been
torn out and destroyed!

07:07.460 --> 07:10.080
But I don't know when it was destroyed!

07:12.210 --> 07:13.500
Retreat!

07:13.500 --> 07:15.290
Retreat to the second defensive line!

07:15.580 --> 07:17.540
Sergeant Malta, cover us!

07:17.540 --> 07:18.670
Roger that.

07:19.170 --> 07:21.830
It's small, but there's no doubt
it's a mature dragon!

07:22.040 --> 07:24.040
It used some sort of magic.

07:25.250 --> 07:28.920
The Winged Monarch, Ultimatia,
can control time.

07:29.460 --> 07:34.380
I'm sure mature dragons
that can use the same powers

07:34.380 --> 07:36.580
will turn up during our upcoming battle.

07:40.130 --> 07:41.130
Time!

07:42.040 --> 07:43.380
Heed me, all creation...

07:43.380 --> 07:44.380
and fall still.

08:07.630 --> 08:09.000
Just as I thought!

08:09.380 --> 08:12.080
We're being attacked while time is stopped!

08:14.130 --> 08:15.750
Major, get away!

08:15.750 --> 08:18.210
You're an indispensable person in this fight!

08:18.210 --> 08:19.000
What?

08:19.000 --> 08:22.000
May you rest in peace.

08:25.170 --> 08:28.540
How can we deal with an enemy
that's breaking the laws of reality?

08:29.000 --> 08:31.170
I'm leaving command of this base to you, Ike!

08:32.540 --> 08:36.500
There is probably a limit on
how long it can stop time.

08:36.500 --> 08:39.290
Otherwise, it would have obliterated us.

08:39.500 --> 08:41.210
And after time has been stopped,

08:41.210 --> 08:44.460
a few seconds must pass
before it can be stopped again.

08:44.790 --> 08:47.040
So we need to attack now!

08:49.380 --> 08:54.460
Each member of the Argentum Corps
is skilled enough to deflect a bullet

08:54.460 --> 08:57.080
as long as time isn't stopped!

08:57.380 --> 08:59.330
You're nothing!

09:07.040 --> 09:08.750
It dodged!

09:10.210 --> 09:11.420
Heed me, all-

09:11.420 --> 09:12.380
Quiet down.

09:16.630 --> 09:20.290
I'll teach you the easiest way
to thwart time stopping.

09:20.290 --> 09:22.080
Lady Ultimatia?

09:22.080 --> 09:25.330
No, why did I think this person
is the progenitor?

09:25.330 --> 09:27.670
Who is... this person?

09:28.040 --> 09:29.250
Catch.

09:31.210 --> 09:32.330
What is that?

09:32.330 --> 09:33.330
A ball?

09:33.330 --> 09:35.630
Should I take it?

09:35.630 --> 09:37.580
Who is that, really?

09:37.580 --> 09:39.170
Wait a second.

09:39.170 --> 09:40.710
I'm not sure what this is.

09:40.710 --> 09:43.580
If I'm not sure, then for now...

09:44.330 --> 09:47.040
Heed me, all creation, and fall still.

09:53.630 --> 09:55.330
S-so hot!

09:55.710 --> 09:57.630
Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot!

09:57.630 --> 09:59.170
Hooooooot!

09:59.380 --> 10:01.580
Light? Why? It's hot!

10:01.580 --> 10:03.380
Why? The sun! Why?

10:03.380 --> 10:07.630
Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot!

10:07.830 --> 10:11.130
It hurts! Hurts! Hurts! Hurts like death!

10:11.130 --> 10:14.630
Hurts like death! Death! Death! Death!

10:23.080 --> 10:24.080
What was that?

10:24.080 --> 10:25.790
Damn it, my eyes!

10:27.710 --> 10:29.750
Are you okay, Major?

10:30.710 --> 10:32.330
That voice...

10:32.330 --> 10:34.130
Crish Weiss?

10:34.130 --> 10:36.880
What in the world just happened?
What about the mature dragon?

10:36.880 --> 10:38.040
I killed it.

10:39.330 --> 10:41.790
This is a white flash-bang.

10:41.790 --> 10:47.000
It's an anti-dragon weapon
that explosively emits stored sunlight.

10:47.210 --> 10:53.080
I modified it so that it will automatically
explode when it senses time has stopped.

10:53.750 --> 10:55.500
Because time is stopped,

10:55.500 --> 10:57.330
they are continually burned by sunlight

10:57.330 --> 10:59.460
that normally would flash
and be gone in an instant.

10:59.460 --> 11:01.710
The agony dominates their thoughts,

11:01.710 --> 11:04.920
and they're unable to process
what's happening.

11:05.250 --> 11:09.710
How do you take down an enemy that
can freely move while time is stopped?

11:10.630 --> 11:15.330
Turn their stilled world
into an unbearable hell.

11:15.330 --> 11:17.210
That's the simplest way.

11:17.960 --> 11:21.170
Crish, we finished setting up the defenses.

11:21.170 --> 11:22.380
Good.

11:22.920 --> 11:25.170
Wait! Whose voice was that just now?

11:25.170 --> 11:27.210
Are there other people here?

11:27.790 --> 11:28.960
You have to ask?

11:28.960 --> 11:30.580
I thought it'd be obvious.

11:30.880 --> 11:35.130
The only other people here,
besides myself and your troops,

11:35.130 --> 11:39.960
are the fifteen hundred civilians
under your protection.

11:39.960 --> 11:41.790
Right, everyone?

11:42.040 --> 11:43.960
That's right, Crish!

11:44.330 --> 11:45.580
What?

11:45.580 --> 11:47.290
They told me,

11:47.290 --> 11:50.250
"We can't stand just waiting around
and twiddling our thumbs anymore!

11:50.250 --> 11:52.290
We want to do something too!

11:52.290 --> 11:55.420
We want to fight alongside
everyone in the corps!"

11:55.710 --> 12:00.920
I was so moved by their pluck
I gave them weapons.

12:00.920 --> 12:03.460
Such a heartwarming display!

12:03.460 --> 12:04.290
That's outrageous!

12:04.460 --> 12:07.750
You can't give civilians weapons
and put them on the battlefield!

12:07.750 --> 12:10.210
That depends on the weapon's properties.

12:10.210 --> 12:13.540
Actually, they were the ones who
just took down the mature dragons.

12:13.540 --> 12:14.920
Anyway,

12:14.920 --> 12:17.080
what is it you're afraid of?

12:17.290 --> 12:20.920
There's nothing to be afraid of.

12:20.920 --> 12:23.290
Don't worry.

12:23.290 --> 12:25.040
We're close to triumphing.

12:25.040 --> 12:26.630
You don't need to doubt.

12:26.630 --> 12:30.210
You're on the path to victory.

12:30.420 --> 12:31.710
Don't worry.

12:31.710 --> 12:34.790
You're feeling very confident.

12:34.790 --> 12:37.420
If we fight together, we'll win.

12:37.880 --> 12:40.500
Olto Zora has already figured out our plan

12:40.500 --> 12:43.210
and will deploy drugged civilians
around the base

12:43.210 --> 12:46.170
to interfere with the teleportation.

12:47.040 --> 12:49.040
What a sicko.

12:49.040 --> 12:52.080
That will double the amount
of magic we'll need.

12:52.080 --> 12:55.330
He'll destroy the corps
before we'll be able to teleport.

12:55.330 --> 12:57.750
What should we do to prevent
that from happening?

12:57.750 --> 12:58.880
That's simple.

12:59.250 --> 13:03.500
Pit that drugged trash against
this hypnotized trash

13:03.500 --> 13:05.580
and let them kill each other!

13:05.580 --> 13:07.130
This is it!

13:07.130 --> 13:08.830
It's time for us to strike back!

13:08.830 --> 13:13.460
Let's rally together our love and courage
and all that wonderful stuff

13:13.460 --> 13:16.170
and let those dragons have it!

13:16.170 --> 13:18.460
Yeah!

13:24.250 --> 13:26.330
Damn it!

13:26.330 --> 13:30.130
There are stupid barriers set up everywhere!

13:33.500 --> 13:35.420
It's freezing!

13:33.500 --> 13:38.330
<b>Thirteenth Seat</b>

13:33.500 --> 13:38.330
<b>Ursh-Gaurun</b>

13:35.750 --> 13:37.670
Not another barrier!

13:37.670 --> 13:40.330
What low-down tricks!

13:40.330 --> 13:41.750
You're being too loud!

13:44.750 --> 13:46.580
Oh, a human!

13:46.580 --> 13:48.000
Perfect!

13:48.380 --> 13:51.330
Take me to the magic circle!

13:51.330 --> 13:54.830
If you do as I say,
I'll allow you to die peacefully!

13:54.830 --> 14:00.540
My stress-induced insomnia is caused by
rowdy dumbasses like you

14:00.540 --> 14:02.750
trying to get to my magic circle!

14:07.460 --> 14:10.460
I need a good night's sleep,
so you gotta die.

14:11.380 --> 14:13.420
The amount of magic required
for the teleportation

14:13.420 --> 14:16.250
equals that of 17,805 inferior dragons?

14:16.460 --> 14:19.750
We could clear out the entire enemy horde,
and it still wouldn't be enough, you moron!

14:19.750 --> 14:21.830
That's just inferior dragons.

14:22.130 --> 14:25.630
Medial dragons have about ten times
the magic of inferior dragons.

14:25.630 --> 14:29.330
Maturing and mature dragons have dozens
to hundreds times the amount of magic.

14:29.330 --> 14:33.330
The stronger the enemy,
the more magic you get from hunting them.

14:33.330 --> 14:35.000
We gotta give this our all.

14:35.290 --> 14:38.040
When the fighting starts, I'm napping.

14:43.080 --> 14:48.670
Why are... Dornea's...

14:49.130 --> 14:52.330
Are you... really...

14:52.580 --> 14:54.420
human?

14:55.580 --> 14:57.880
I'm taking yours too.

15:04.830 --> 15:09.670
Good thing I managed to dispose of him
while I had control.

15:10.420 --> 15:11.960
Master Fu!

15:12.130 --> 15:14.500
Come to your senses!

15:16.580 --> 15:17.460
Master Fu!

15:17.460 --> 15:19.080
Did your right arm take over?

15:19.080 --> 15:20.670
Knock it off! That's friggin' cold!

15:20.670 --> 15:22.170
We'll help you now! Blasted right arm!

15:22.170 --> 15:23.670
Release our friend, Master Fu,
from your clutches!

15:23.670 --> 15:25.830
We can't! Freeze it! Freeze it!

15:27.290 --> 15:28.750
You donkeys are gonna kill me!

15:28.750 --> 15:29.830
Master Fu!

15:29.830 --> 15:32.250
You've been freed from
your right arm's control!

15:32.250 --> 15:34.420
I wasn't under its control
in the first place, idiot!

15:34.420 --> 15:35.460
What?

15:35.460 --> 15:38.880
We were convinced you were
because Miss Majo said so!

15:41.710 --> 15:43.130
Hey, uggo.

15:43.130 --> 15:46.000
You were using the chaos as a diversion
so you could try to kill me!

15:46.000 --> 15:48.920
N-no! I sweah I wuzn't!

15:49.210 --> 15:53.540
Never in my dreams would trying to become
Chief Thaumaturge by murdering y-

15:54.130 --> 15:56.580
Please calm down, Master Fu!

15:56.580 --> 15:59.750
Us outcasts must stick together!

16:00.380 --> 16:01.960
Incredible!

16:01.960 --> 16:04.710
He took down that Thirteenth Seat alone.

16:04.710 --> 16:06.710
And using that magic too...

16:06.880 --> 16:08.880
Sure enough, this corps is something else!

16:08.880 --> 16:10.420
What a treasure trove of talent!

16:10.420 --> 16:12.250
Now I want them even more.

16:12.500 --> 16:15.630
I want to gain control of them with
the least amount of damage possible.

16:15.630 --> 16:17.330
In order to do that...

16:20.330 --> 16:22.130
Tree roots?

16:24.710 --> 16:26.130
Everyone, hurry!

16:26.130 --> 16:27.040
This way!

16:27.040 --> 16:29.380
Master Crish!

16:33.000 --> 16:36.380
Why are you dragging civilians around?

16:36.380 --> 16:38.210
And what's with the guns?

16:38.210 --> 16:39.460
I'll explain later!

16:39.880 --> 16:43.130
The pressure from the forest is starting
to overwhelm the princess's barriers!

16:44.710 --> 16:46.790
We need to fortify the magic circle's defenses!

16:46.790 --> 16:49.500
If it gets destroyed, it's all over for us!

16:50.750 --> 16:52.460
Hurry up, commander.

16:52.460 --> 16:55.460
We don't have as much time as we thought!

17:02.250 --> 17:03.710
Dragon coming from below!

17:03.710 --> 17:04.670
Fan out!

17:08.330 --> 17:10.210
Greya! Let's give it a whirl.

17:10.210 --> 17:11.210
Let's do it.

17:15.880 --> 17:17.830
Slaughter! Slaughter!

17:21.460 --> 17:22.250
Nyo?

17:22.250 --> 17:23.540
They're coming from above?

17:28.830 --> 17:31.080
How? Nyo nyo?

17:31.080 --> 17:32.830
Master Zora, give us orders! Master Zo-!

17:32.830 --> 17:35.210
Knock it off with that "nyo" crap,
you muppet!

17:35.540 --> 17:37.080
Wow!

17:37.460 --> 17:40.420
I did not anticipate that she'd
fire her troops like cannonballs,

17:40.420 --> 17:43.420
and they'd break through barriers
using their own power.

17:43.580 --> 17:46.080
That's just absurd.

17:46.080 --> 17:48.670
That should be fatal.

17:50.250 --> 17:52.540
No, I understand.

17:52.920 --> 17:57.040
The more insane the commander is,
the more insane the troops are.

17:58.670 --> 17:59.880
Commander!

17:59.880 --> 18:01.920
We took care of the fire-breathing one!

18:01.920 --> 18:03.540
But the spikey one isn't here!

18:03.540 --> 18:05.750
He's probably on the cliff!

18:06.500 --> 18:07.750
I'll launch you one more time!

18:07.750 --> 18:09.750
Are you guys ready?

18:11.210 --> 18:13.130
Sacrificing itself by jumping from above?

18:13.420 --> 18:14.830
Damn i-

18:18.580 --> 18:20.290
Sorry,

18:20.290 --> 18:22.710
but I've dethroned your air supremacy.

18:23.000 --> 18:26.290
Your senses have slowly dulled.

18:26.290 --> 18:28.000
That's only natural.

18:28.000 --> 18:30.130
You have no practical experience
with large-scale battles,

18:30.130 --> 18:32.250
but you managed the defense
and command yourself,

18:32.250 --> 18:36.330
as well as the offense,
with an overwhelming disadvantage.

18:36.670 --> 18:41.540
You didn't realize how quickly
that would exhaust you.

18:41.960 --> 18:47.040
Being able to do anything you set
your mind to has its disadvantages.

18:50.420 --> 18:53.170
It's been fun, but the party's over.

18:53.500 --> 18:54.830
Comrade,

18:54.830 --> 18:56.920
it's not over yet.

18:57.250 --> 18:59.920
Three hundred meters behind me.

18:59.920 --> 19:01.630
Verify it for yourself now.

19:08.830 --> 19:13.460
A third of my army has already been lost.

19:13.460 --> 19:16.250
If we push with numbers,
we will crush them eventually.

19:16.250 --> 19:18.790
My assessment remains unchanged.

19:19.210 --> 19:22.580
But the number required for that
is higher than expected.

19:23.130 --> 19:24.960
We must address this.

19:31.130 --> 19:34.920
There's not even time to catch my breath!

19:35.830 --> 19:38.670
We cannot even get close to Taratectra!

19:38.670 --> 19:39.920
There's so many!

19:39.920 --> 19:41.880
There are too many for us!

19:42.460 --> 19:43.710
But...

19:44.000 --> 19:46.210
He just won't give in!

19:51.420 --> 19:54.420
Burn!

19:54.880 --> 19:58.880
How is he still holding on like that
when he already has one foot in the grave?

19:59.170 --> 20:02.630
If he ain't stopping,
I sure as hell can't stop!

20:04.750 --> 20:07.250
I can't... breathe.

20:08.830 --> 20:09.920
It hurts.

20:09.920 --> 20:11.750
It's so painful. So cold.

20:11.750 --> 20:13.380
I just want to stop.

20:13.790 --> 20:15.210
No, I can't!

20:15.710 --> 20:18.710
Because I've been given
the mightiest of powers.

20:19.290 --> 20:21.040
I gotta hunt Taratectra,

20:21.040 --> 20:22.750
hunt Olto Zora,

20:22.750 --> 20:24.630
hunt dragon hordes,

20:24.630 --> 20:26.210
and gather magic.

20:26.210 --> 20:28.540
I'll protect everyone! By myself!

20:28.960 --> 20:33.330
I have to so no one else will die!

20:34.210 --> 20:37.500
By myself, I'll protect everything...

20:39.290 --> 20:41.330
You can't just show up late

20:41.330 --> 20:43.380
and act like you're the hero!

20:45.130 --> 20:48.130
What he said felt like a punch in the gut.

20:49.380 --> 20:52.210
I was a little relieved to hear him say that.

20:53.290 --> 20:55.920
But that was surely...

20:55.920 --> 20:57.420
weakness.

20:57.750 --> 20:59.750
I always survived.

20:59.960 --> 21:02.130
I'm the only one who survives.

21:02.460 --> 21:06.000
I can only be with people

21:06.000 --> 21:08.250
whose deaths won't hurt me

21:08.250 --> 21:10.460
or people who won't die.

21:12.830 --> 21:14.250
What a familiar feeling.

21:28.540 --> 21:29.540
What?

21:29.540 --> 21:31.170
He's on death's door...

21:31.170 --> 21:33.380
but his techniques are even sharper!

21:36.000 --> 21:37.540
I see.

21:37.540 --> 21:39.500
Apparently, I miscalculated.

21:39.500 --> 21:43.290
That happens on the battlefield occasionally.

21:43.880 --> 21:45.630
This shit stain is persistent.

21:47.000 --> 21:48.500
That's strange...

21:49.830 --> 21:53.500
A desperate plight where
defeat seems certain.

21:53.500 --> 21:55.250
A daily occurrence in my future.

21:57.330 --> 21:59.580
Now, more than ever before...

21:59.580 --> 22:02.790
I sense my future self is close.

22:07.170 --> 22:09.750
I've once again returned to hell.
